{
 "name": "Justus v. Principi, Dec 22, 1992, 5 Vet.App. 510 (1992)",
 "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center\">\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Decision Assessment Document<br />\tJustus v. Principi,&nbsp;Dec 22, 1992,&nbsp;5 Vet.App. 510 (1992)<br />\tU.S. Court of Appeals for Veterans Claims (Court)</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>What the case is about:&nbsp;</strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">The Court held that the ultimate credibility or weight of the evidence should be presumed initially, for the limited purpose of reopening the claim.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>Impact on VBA:&nbsp;</strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">The Court's holding has been incorporated into the Manual M21-1, III.iv.2.B.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>Summary of the facts and Court\u2019s reasons:&nbsp;</strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Service connection had been denied for a heart murmur noted at separation, as a residual of possible childhood rheumatic fever apparently.&nbsp; A medical opinion was submitted for reopening, which indicated that the murmur more likely developed due to an undiagnosed episode of rheumatic fever during active duty, based on a history of repeated sore throat and chest cold symptoms provided by the veteran.&nbsp; This opinion was not considered new and material by the BVA, because it relied on history conveyed by the veteran rather than on a review of contemporaneous clinical records.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>References:&nbsp;</strong></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">CAVC case number: No. 91-1596</span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://vbaw.vba.va.gov/bl/21/advisory/CAVCDAD.htm#bmj\" target=\"_blank\">http://vbaw.vba.va.gov/bl/21/advisory/CAVCDAD.htm#bmj</a></span></span></p><p>\t<span style=\"font-size: 14px\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><a class=\"eGainArticleLink\" articleid=\"554400000015808\" articlename=\"M21-1, Part III, Subpart iv, Chapter 2, Section B - Historical\" href=\"https://www.knowva.ebenefits.va.gov/system/ws/v11/ss/article/554400000015808?portalId=554400000001018&usertype=customer&\">M21-1, Part III, Subpart iv, Chapter 2, Section B - Revision of Decisions</a></span></span></p><p>\t&nbsp;</p>",
